### Guidelines for generating the PR:
1. **Language (mandatory):** The PR **title** and **entire body** must be in **English** — professional, concise, and consistent with the rest of the repo. Never default to Portuguese or another language because of chat context or author preference, unless the user **explicitly** requests another language for that specific PR.
2. **Holistic Analysis:** Analyze the **entire diff** as a single block. Ignore chat history/incremental steps.
3. **PR title:** Use Conventional Commits: `type(scope): short imperative summary`. If a Jira key exists (from branch or commits), treat it as **context in scope** in **lowercase**: e.g. key `ABC-123` → title `feat(abc-123): ebdb_agent prospect tables and qualification layer`. The summary must still describe **what** changed (DAG, area, behavior); do not let the ticket replace the subject. Do **not** append `(ABC-123)` at the end of the title or use a standalone `##` heading for the ticket.
4. **Jira in the body:** Do **not** use a top-level `##` heading for the ticket. When a key exists, add a **second bullet** under **Why?** with the Jira tracker link (see skeleton below). Omit that bullet entirely if there is no ticket.
5. **Why Section:** First bullet = **purpose/value**. Second bullet (when applicable) = Jira tracker link only. **Do not** describe deep technical implementation here.
6. **What Section:** List actual changes from the **full diff**, ordered by impact.
7. **Attention Points:** Use `### !Attention Points!` **only** for risks or **pending** tasks (style/docs/tests). For a **new** PR, **omit** the section if there is nothing material to flag. When **updating** an existing PR, if the current body already contains `### !Attention Points!` with content, **preserve that block verbatim** — do not delete it when regenerating **Why?** / **What?** / **How everything was tested?**.
8. **Strict Omission:** Do not use bare **N/A**, “TBD”, or meta-commentary in **Why?**, **What?**, **How everything was tested?**, or **!Attention Points!** — omit empty subsections or bullets instead. **Exception:** the **Screenshots** subsection (rule 9) may use a short **English** placeholder such as *N/A — author to confirm or attach visuals* where a manual follow-up is intentional.
9. **Screenshots (always keep the heading):** Always include `#### Screenshots` after **How everything was tested?** When **creating** a PR or when the existing PR body has **no** Screenshots block yet, add the subsection with the **canonical placeholder bullet** from the skeleton below (English; signals a manual step for the author). When **updating** an existing PR, if `#### Screenshots` is already filled with **real content** (e.g. image links, uploaded assets, or descriptive bullets that are not only the placeholder), **preserve that entire block verbatim** when regenerating the rest of the description. If the existing block is empty or only repeats the placeholder, you may replace it with a fresh placeholder.
10. **No dropped sections (updates):** When **updating** an existing PR description, fetch the current GitHub body first. Regenerate in English only the core blocks **`### Why?`**, **`### What?`**, and **`### How everything was tested?`** (with **`#### Screenshots`** per rule 9). **Do not remove** any other topic the author already had: copy **verbatim** — in **the same order they appeared** — every remaining section, including at least **`### Checklist before opening the PR!`** (keep all `- [ ]` / `- [x]` states and links), **`### !Attention Points!`** (rule 7), and any other custom `### …` block (e.g. team notes). **Never** drop a heading that was present in the previous body unless the user explicitly asks to remove it.
11. **Checklist on new PRs:** For a **new** PR (no prior body), always end the description with **`### Checklist before opening the PR!`** using the bullet list from **`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`** (default **unchecked** `- [ ]` unless the author has already confirmed every item).
12. **Clean Output:** Remove all instructional text and bracketed hints from the final response **except** the intentional Screenshots placeholder line and the real checklist lines from the template, which stay until the author edits them.

